@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Student
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Settings
@inject IStudentProfileService ProfileService

@*
    StudentProfilePage — "הפרופיל שלי"

    VISUAL SOURCE OF TRUTH
    design-reference/motiva-student-final/Motiva Student Profile final.dc.html.
    It supersedes the older design-reference/motiva/project/Motiva Profile.dc.html
    this page was previously built from.

    The screen opens on the shared white page header ("הפרופיל שלי") and then a
    TWO-COLUMN grid, 1.6fr / 1fr:

        ┌──────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┐
        │ פרטים אישיים        (opaque)     │ הצוות שלי        (translucent)│
        │ העדפות             (translucent) │ שירותים מחוברים  (translucent)│
        └──────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘

    There is NO identity hero row and NO avatar on this screen any more. The
    name and role that row drew were redundant (the header names the page,
    פרטים אישיים states the name in its own fields), and the profile does not
    use an editable profile image (the top nav already shows the user's avatar),
    so the whole row — avatar included — was removed. The page now runs straight
    from the white header into the content grid, which stretches to fill the
    available viewport height (see the .spf-content / .spf-grid flex rules).

    The wide column carries what the student edits about themselves; the
    narrow one carries the two read-mostly blocks about everything else.
    That proportion is the reference's, and it is also what keeps the
    personal-details card's two field columns at a readable measure without
    a page-level max-width.

    ── WHERE THE REFERENCE IS PROTOTYPE DATA, AND WHAT IS RENDERED INSTEAD ──
    Its user, team, email addresses, "מכינת עתיד, מחזור 2026" and connected
    Google account are demo values. Nothing here copies them:

      * identity + פרטים אישיים   GET /api/student/me (StudentProfileDto)
      * העדפות                    GET/PUT /api/users/me/notification-preferences
      * הצוות שלי                 GET /api/projects/my-context (already cached
                                  by the shell — this page adds no request)
      * שירותים מחוברים           GET /api/google-calendar/status + the real
                                  OAuth connect / disconnect endpoints

    ── WHAT THE REFERENCE DRAWS THAT THE PRODUCT CANNOT BACK ────────────────
    Reported rather than invented — see the per-card headers for the detail:

      * an editable "שם מלא". PUT /api/student/me updates users.Phone and
        nothing else, so the name is rendered read-only.
      * three of its four preference toggles ("תזכורות לפני מפגשים",
        "סיכום שבועי באימייל", "סנכרון אירועים ליומן Google"). No
        NotificationType, no scheduler and no per-user sync flag backs any of
        them — see StudentProfileNotificationsCard.
      * a "תפקיד" field. The role is real; a read-only field repeating it would
        be a field in appearance only. שנה אקדמית takes that slot instead.

    The avatar and its upload / remove controls (PUT/DELETE /api/student/me/avatar,
    Student-gated) are no longer surfaced here — the profile does not present an
    editable profile image. The endpoints are untouched server-side; only this
    view stopped drawing the control.

    ── TWO OF THE FOUR CARDS ARE NOT THIS SCREEN'S ANY MORE ────────────────
    העדפות and שירותים מחוברים moved to Pages/Settings as
    ProfileNotificationsCard / ProfileIntegrationsCard, because neither was
    ever a student's: both read endpoints that are gated by no role, and the
    Lecturer / Mentor profile now renders the same two instances. The move was
    a rename and a namespace, nothing else — the markup, the scoped styles and
    the behaviour are unchanged, so this page renders exactly what it did
    before. The card's own copy is the only thing that varies by role, and
    ProfileNotificationsCard takes it as a parameter whose default is this
    screen's wording.

    Not routable: SettingsPage.razor owns /settings and renders this for
    students only. Mentor / Lecturer / Admin get StaffProfilePage.
*@

@* The approved white Core page-header. The page title reads "הפרופיל שלי" —
   the identity hero below states WHO the profile belongs to (name, avatar,
   role), so the two do not repeat: this is the page-level frame, that is the
   profile content. *@
<MPageHeaderCard Title="הפרופיל שלי" Scale="MPageHeaderCard.HeaderScale.Core" />

@if (_loading)
{
    <div class="spf-page-state">
        <span class="spf-page-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>טוענת פרטים…</span>
    </div>
}
else if (_profile is null)
{
    <div class="spf-page-state">
        <MEmptyState Live="true"
                     Title="אירעה שגיאה בטעינת הפרופיל"
                     Description="נסי לרענן את הדף." />
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div class="spf-content">
    <div class="spf-grid">
        @* Each column is a plain flex stack, exactly as in the reference —
           the two sections in a column are siblings at the same 18px rhythm
           as the gap between the columns themselves. *@
        <div class="spf-col">
            <StudentProfilePersonalCard Profile="_profile"
                                        OnProfileChanged="StateHasChanged" />
            <ProfileNotificationsCard />
        </div>

        <div class="spf-col">
            <StudentProfileTeamCard Profile="_profile" />
            <ProfileIntegrationsCard />
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    private StudentProfileDto? _profile;
    private bool _loading = true;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _profile = await ProfileService.GetProfileAsync();
        _loading = false;
    }
}
